From 4f33aac8b5a493b16fa6be1996df2d8507a51a9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wip(F30#0): make the retained capture-offer path work for
 ordinary catches (verification running)

Found while driving ordinary canonical catches through the capture_offer
path (alpha-only until now, never shipped on):
- the capture roster guard compared raw encoded cards with the owner
  projection, which since 187a3f24 carries no in-fight energy meter; it
  now compares that projection (energy dropped on both sides) and
  tolerates passive care accrued since the stage (merge_owner_passive);
- the staged newcomer card is the energy-free owner projection, and the
  owner install re-adds an empty meter only to decode it;
- a catch with a free slot is kept directly: no release-ceremony screen
  (which left GameMenu owning input); the ceremony stays for a full belt.
Fixtures (exception (a)): smoke_party_count_after_catches binds its live
world to TEST_SLOT (catches now journal world rows) and waits, bounded,
for the async install; smoke_catching sets current_scene as the shipping
boot does and waits for the install. Assertions unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FeyS6dDcmbbPiVs7C8wXsC
